{"id":59847593244658,"type":"album","name":"Eagles","artist":"Eagles","year":1972,"weight":20,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711100.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-150e50b2-570b-456a-baf4-0da3437d19bd/mbid-150e50b2-570b-456a-baf4-0da3437d19bd-6643477329.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":10,"country":"DE","yt":"32Oc2d_3yEk","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/eagles/eagles"},"desc":"Eagles is the debut album by the rock band of the same name, released in 1972. The album was recorded at London's Olympic Studios with producer Glyn Johns. The album was an immediate success for the young band reaching #22 on the charts and going platinum. The album also released three Top 40 singles with \"Take it Easy\", \"Witchy Woman\" and \"Peaceful Easy Feeling\". The three singles reached #12, #9 and #22 respectively. The album played a major role in popularizing the southern California country rock sound. In 2003, the album was ranked number 374 on Rolling Stone magazine's list ."},"artist_ref":{"id":106115726467187,"name":"The Eagles","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/178be204025c8d38a72113564b647baf/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":90510611927654,"type":"genre","name":"Country Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":425,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":251671925246370,"type":"genre","name":"Soft Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":418,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":133646791193319,"type":"genre","name":"Laurel Canyon Scene","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":200,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":177455037556203,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Laurel Canyon Scene","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":178,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":36565743209502,"name":"Rolling Stone 500 Greatest Albums Of All Time 2023 Edition","src":"musthear","grp":null,"list_year":null,"rank":207,"year":null,"note":null,"total":500,"scaruffi":null},{"id":1929347509